# Citations whose referent is REAL but structurally invisible from this tree.
#
# This file is not an excuse list. An entry must say why the referent cannot be
# seen here, and the bar is EXISTENCE CONFIRMED ELSEWHERE, not plausibility.
#
# The distinction, learned 2026-09-04: a citation of something in the private
# monorepo is exempt only once someone has gone and looked, and the entry
# records where it was found (file:line). A citation nobody has checked is a
# finding — and that day the check paid for itself, because 19 Lean citations
# that "plausibly existed in the monorepo" turned out to exist nowhere at all,
# while one cross-repo test citation turned out to be real.
#
# So: never add an entry to quiet the tool. Add it after confirming, and say
# who/what confirmed it.
#
# Format:  name  # reason
insecure_random_get  # WASI ABI import name (paired with secure_random), not an in-repo symbol
repcode_d3r3_5q      # benchmark circuit under gitignored fixes/ (perf-baseline-m5max-20260818.txt)
omega_pattern_cross_wire_golden  # verified 2026-09-04 to exist at quantum-core/src/backends/omega.rs:792 (inline #[test] in the private monorepo); cited from here by file:line

# --- Added 2026-09-04 when the identifier pass grew a markdown arm. ---
# All six were inspected individually; none was a false claim. Kept as
# allowlist entries rather than doc edits because each name is correct as
# written for its audience.
circuit_to_pattern   # quantum-core public API, confirmed at quantum-core/src/mbqc/compile.rs:207, re-exported mbqc/mod.rs:34
cpuinfo_max_freq     # Linux sysfs node (/sys/.../cpufreq/cpuinfo_max_freq), an OS interface this repo reads, not defines
pbi_start_tvsec      # macOS proc_bsdinfo struct field, named by PROTOCOL.md as part of the wire spec it defines
wide_chain_19q       # benchmark circuit under gitignored fixes/ (PLAN-MPS-FIX ledger)
grover_generic_28q   # benchmark circuit under gitignored fixes/ (PLAN-SV-PERF ledger)
xy_model_20q         # benchmark circuit under gitignored fixes/ (PLAN-SV-PERF ledger)

# --- Added 2026-09-05. Surfaced by the wildcard/markdown arm after the
# "CLOSED, exits 0" ledger line was written — the ledger was wrong for a day.
create_single_mode_squeezing_matrix  # piquasso (external oracle), confirmed at piquasso/_math/gate_matrices.py:93 on upstream main (github Budapest-Quantum-Computing-Group/piquasso); FIXES_PLAN.md:2152 cites it with its file path, as an oracle's behaviour not an in-repo symbol. Checked against main, not the 8.0.1 tag.
